WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.258
Day 4. Two letters the same in the middle.

2
00:00:02.708 --> 00:00:09.520
Watch first. The first one on the page is done for you: show it, do the next one together, and your child does the rest.

3
00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:13.613
When two letters in the middle are the same, the word splits between them.

4
00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:20.819
The word is rabbit.

5
00:00:27.132 --> 00:00:28.175
The word is kitten.

6
00:00:29.075 --> 00:00:36.657
In some words the second beat sounds a little softer than it looks. If your child reads it as written, the real word usually comes.

7
00:00:37.107 --> 00:00:41.663
The words to say to your child are in the yellow box at the top. Read them out.

8
00:00:42.113 --> 00:00:46.637
Read the first row of job one together. Your child reads the second row.

9
00:00:47.087 --> 00:00:51.119
If a word goes wrong, do not say it. Say the same words every time.

10
00:00:51.569 --> 00:00:56.297
Cover the second beat with a finger. Read the first one. Then uncover the rest.

11
00:00:57.097 --> 00:01:02.670
For job two, press play for your child and step away. The voice waits, then says each word.

12
00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:06.583
At the end, your child reads three words to you. Mark each one.
